From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] sim: report the card slots when there is no card

GetProperties returned only Present while no card was in the active
slot, so CardSlotCount and ActiveCardSlot disappeared exactly when a
client needed them.

A modem with one logical slot and several physical ones, such as a SIM
slot and an eUICC, is mapped to one physical slot at a time. Mapped to
the empty one, it has no card, and the only way to reach the card that
is there is to set ActiveCardSlot. Setting it already works with no
card present; reading it did not. A client that cannot see more than
one slot cannot offer the switch, and the eUICC stays out of reach.

Seen on a Pixel 3a (sargo, HIDL radio): mapped to the empty nano-SIM
slot, EuiccManager.OpenChannel failed with the radio's INTERNAL_ERR,
SimManager reported only Present: false, and the Settings app hid its
slot switcher. Setting ActiveCardSlot to 2 by hand brought the eUICC
back on the first try.

The slots describe the modem, not the card, so report them before the
Present check, and say so in the API document.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 doc/sim-api.txt |  8 ++++++++
 src/sim.c       | 17 +++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/sim-api.txt b/doc/sim-api.txt
index c8b7a2b..e4faf84 100644
--- a/doc/sim-api.txt
+++ b/doc/sim-api.txt
@@ -235,3 +235,11 @@ Properties	boolean Present [readonly]
 
 			This property will range from 1 (default) to
 			CardSlotCount (max) value.
+
+			CardSlotCount and ActiveCardSlot describe the modem,
+			not the card, so they are reported, and ActiveCardSlot
+			can be set, while Present is false. The active slot
+			may be the empty one on a modem with a single logical
+			slot and several physical ones, such as a SIM slot and
+			an eUICC; setting ActiveCardSlot is then the way to
+			reach the card.
diff --git a/src/sim.c b/src/sim.c
index 2790c02..857e372 100644
--- a/src/sim.c
+++ b/src/sim.c
@@ -486,6 +486,17 @@ static DBusMessage *sim_get_properties(DBusConnection *conn,
 
 	ofono_dbus_dict_append(&dict, "Present", DBUS_TYPE_BOOLEAN, &present);
 
+	/*
+	 * The slots describe the modem, not the card, and an empty active
+	 * slot is exactly when a client needs them: setting ActiveCardSlot
+	 * is the only way to move to a slot that does have a card in it.
+	 */
+	ofono_dbus_dict_append(&dict, "CardSlotCount", DBUS_TYPE_UINT32,
+							&sim->card_slot_count);
+
+	ofono_dbus_dict_append(&dict, "ActiveCardSlot", DBUS_TYPE_UINT32,
+							&sim->active_card_slot);
+
 	if (!present)
 		goto done;
 
@@ -555,12 +566,6 @@ static DBusMessage *sim_get_properties(DBusConnection *conn,
 	ofono_dbus_dict_append_dict(&dict, "Retries", DBUS_TYPE_BYTE,
 							&pin_retries_dict);
 
-	ofono_dbus_dict_append(&dict, "CardSlotCount", DBUS_TYPE_UINT32,
-							&sim->card_slot_count);
-
-	ofono_dbus_dict_append(&dict, "ActiveCardSlot", DBUS_TYPE_UINT32,
-							&sim->active_card_slot);
-
 	g_free(pin_retries_dict);
 	g_free(dbus_retries);
 
